in 2019 Tesla revealed their  much-anticipated pick up the Cyber truck  even though it looks like something out  of a science fiction film The Cyber  truck is just about ready to hit our  streets in 2023 and when it does it will  shake up the pickup truck market today I  will tell you everything you need to  know about Tesla's much-awaited cyber  truck performance first the Cyber truck  comes in three different performance  configurations the single motor  rear-wheel drive the dual motor and the  tri-motor before exploring anything else  let's look at these performance  configurations and their meaning the  first one the single motor rear wheel  drive will be able to get from 0 to 60  miles in 6.5 seconds with an estimated  250 miles on a single charge and in true  pickup style this version of the Cyber  truck will be able to tow over 7 500  pounds then there is the dual motor  hitting 0 to 60 miles in 4.5 seconds and  able to tow weights that are over 10 000  pounds finally the tri-motor which is by  far the most powerful cyber truck hit 60  miles in 2.9 seconds this cyber truck  configuration will also be able to tow  up to 14 000 pounds at about 500 miles  on a single charge these versions will  come with independent rear steering  wheels meaning that you can steer all  four wheels making it easier to travel  in all kinds of terrain but that's not  all Tesla will also offer each car owner  the option to upgrade to its new  autonomous FSD or fully self-driving  feature at an added cost say what you  will about the Cyber truck but I'm  already hooked exterior so what else  makes the Cyber truck special well after  it was first announced the Cyber truck  received mixed feelings mostly because  of how it is shaped nobody outside of  Tesla knew at the time that its angular  look and basic body panel lines were  that way because the exterior material  was too hard to shape and may break the  gigafactory stamping press if they tried  to give it a different shape and if  you're wondering why Tesla doesn't just  change the material so they can make  differently shaped cyber trucks you're  probably not the first person I'm here  to tell you that there are good reasons  for you using that material the exterior  shell is made out of a stainless steel  alloy named the ultra hard 30X cold  rolled stainless steel which was created  by Tesla initially for their SpaceX  Starship shell it is said to be  bulletproof strong resistant to  corrosion and be able to withstand  temperatures in both the hot and cold  extremes with such a strong body the  Cyber truck may be the safest pickup for  passengers in Collision accidents  recently though Elon announced that the  Starship would be using 304l stainless  steel which is just as sturdy so we can  expect cyber truck to move in that  direction in the future additionally  since its release independent studies of  the design have revealed that the truck  shape is aerodynamically significant as  well giving the Cyber truck a drag  coefficient of around 0.39 which is  impressive because most pickup trucks  feature in the 0.45 to 0.55 range so I  guess there is a method to the madness  behind this sci-fi look interior we now  take a look at the inside to appreciate  the interior of the Cyber truck which is  nothing like its in industrial exterior  its dashboard is made of compressed  paper and the Finish is made to have a  lavish marble appearance I bet you  didn't expect that huh well this aligns  with Tesla's commitment to  sustainability following in the  proverbial footsteps of the model 3  which was announced to be moving to a  completely leather-free interior  ultimately Tesla hopes to have all its  Vehicles made of sustainable interior  materials in the future but back to the  Cyber trucks interior the luxuriously  minimalist dashboard only hosts a  17-inch Center touchscreen with controls  for every truck's function the yolk  style steering wheel shares its design  pedigree with the model S plaid and will  have similar functionalities built in by  way of two control Wheels in terms of  space and number of Passengers The Cyber  truck can seat six people with a  spacious cargo hold at the back one of  the unique features of the Cyber truck  is the cargo hold cover which is also  made out of armor glass that is so  strong that it can hold the full weight  of Elon standing over it though I don't  know why anyone would want to stand over  it and as always over engineering is  what you get from Tesla anyway but I  suspect that they might use this cover  to host a solar panel in the future to  self-charge the truck now that would be  a neat use of the feature for sure  mirrors even though the Cyber truck has  all these incredible features it lacks  some more traditional features I bet you  noticed the missing side mirrors and  rear view mirrors well instead of  mirrors the Cyber truck uses cameras and  a screen to show you a live video feed  of what is outside the vehicle having no  rear view mirror in favor of a camera is  nothing new but the absence of side  mirrors is not yet allowed in the United  States simply put the version of the  Cyber truck that was displayed at the  unveiling with no side mirrors can't be  driven in the US at least until the  regulations change but that's not the  end for that design in Europe however  there is already the Audi e-tron with  cameras instead of mirrors so the  mirrorless cyber truck could be  available there while the US is still  updating vehicle regulations for now it  seems like Tesla is waiting to hear what  the final ruling will be on that before  they make their mirrorless design  official so you can expect the first  versions of the Cyber truck rolling out  of its Texas Factory to have the side  mirrors installed on them floating  abilities something that won't need  regulation change is a truck's ability  to float Elon has claimed that the Cyber  truck can drive through water and float  during flooded conditions when he called  submarines underwater electric vehicles  he used that to back up his claim that  Tesla cars can work as boats for short  periods of time because they have no air  intakes much like submarines with a  video from Shanghai making the rounds  sometime Back featuring a Tesla Model 3  traversing through flood waters musk may  be onto something with his claims the  Cyber truck looks more like a  utilitarian vehicle in this regard  especially with global warming causing  many water-related natural disasters  worldwide  supercharge another thing that makes  Tesla unique is that all of their  vehicles are electric vehicles and the  Cyber truck is not about to change that  the Cyber truck will be charged at Tesla  Supercharger stations still because of  its size and power it is being built its  own supercharging stations as the  existing ones get a refurbishment as  well the new superchargers dubbed V3  have an impressive one megawatt cabinet  that supports a rate of up to 250  kilowatts per vehicle and these aren't  even the Cyber truck superchargers for  the Cyber truck there has been mention  of V4 superchargers which are expected  to reach charging rates of up to 350  kilowatts looks like Tesla is rightfully  preparing for this powerful vehicle in  all the ways that matter battery to make  sure that the Cyber truck battery can  withstand the power that the  supercharger will provide the Cyber  truck battery will have to be upgraded  from what Tesla's been using all along  the Cybertron battery will be massive  with the entire pack at 200 to 250  kilowatt hours double the current Tesla  battery size if you remember the  performance numbers from earlier this  huge battery will make perfect sense for  a machine as big as the Cyber truck to  function that way requires equally great  power but the power of the battery  doesn't have to be reflected physically  that's why Tesla is experimenting with  prototypes that could be significantly  lighter in weight but still have great  energy storage range and an even greater  increase in power up to six times to be  exact if this is successful the weight  reduction will make the Cyber truck's  high power requirements a step closer to  reality thermal regulation now with all  those improvements to make the battery  more efficient thermal regulation could  be an enemy of such progress this might  be an obvious feature for any other  vehicle owner but for electric vehicles  it can affect a single charger's range  with losses of up to 40 percent in cold  weather Tesla intends to guard against  that by using a heat pump on the Cyber  truck making it the second vehicle after  the model y the model-wide's heat pump  works through a motorized octal valve to  transfer and distribute coolant for  thermal regulation of components and  Passengers The Cyber truck heat pump  technology will be more efficient with  its range unaffected even in cold  weather when the heat is turned up  frequently this thermal management  system is so sophisticated that it has  been likened to that of a jet engine  meaning that once again Elon Musk is  changing another industry one Innovation  at a time other features if that was all  the Innovation that the cyber trunk has  it would be enough but there are still  more more of the features that we can  expect from the Cyber truck include an  improved air suspension with Active Ride  height and active damping systems for  those who may not be familiar with these  the Active Ride height is a system that  allows for a vehicle to vary its ground  clearance this can be done to give  better ground clearance over rough  terrain which the Cyber truck can expect  to frequent like all other pickup trucks  the active damping system on the other  hand is a feature that automatically  adjusts suspension stiffness or softness  in different driving situations or  terrains this feature can make a ride  smoother by absorbing Road bumps or make  it more thrilling depending on how you  drive it is especially important to  vehicles that are meant to be driven on  all kinds of terrain because it gives  the driver more control I'm sure there  are various other features of the Cyber  truck that'll come out once the cars are  actually delivered to owners but until  then I'll keep scouring the forums to  bring you all the updates on what  promises to be a game-changing vehicle  for both Tesla and the automotive  industry as a whole well that's all I  have for you today so what do you think  of the Cyber truck do you think it is  worth all the hype let me know in the  comment section below and if you enjoyed  this video hit the Subscribe button and  continue watching our videos by clicking  on one of the cards on your screen see  you in the next one
 

